  {
    "episode_id": 48869,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/8/48869.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. Well, yeah, it's somewhat very respectful of the great achievements of many in academics. I would say sports and competitive sports is much more indicative of what life is really like than what we see in the ivory tower. And so I think that sports are a great way to learn about leadership and to learn about resilience and to learn what it takes to achieve And that was really what sports did for me. Particularly at the college level, one of my coaches at Army at West Point in wrestling was a man who had won the Olympic gold medal as a wrestler. And seeing the difference of what it took to be able to compete at his level, and that was inspiration for me, the level of dedication. And then, listen, sports, there's nowhere to hide.",
