    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/8/48869.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 15,
    "turn_text": "And so moving on to, I mean, foreign policy is kind of one of your main issues. You've worked on it at the highest levels of government. You've been talking about it a lot on the campaign trail. Just to kind of kick us off with a very broad question about it, one thing that I noticed working in DC is there is sort of a group of people who started off with their interest being in foreign policy and then realized, oh my gosh, there's so much wrong at home on the domestic front. What's the point of projecting American power if the state of affairs on home turf is so bad? What in your view is kind of the utility of focusing so much on foreign policy is there as much of a distinction between foreign and domestic as a lot of people think?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
