    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/8/48869.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 18,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, it's such a great example of the point because when I run across commonwealth of Pennsylvania, I'm talking to voters on the ground, whether they're in rural Pennsylvania or in the metropolitan areas. This fentanyl crisis is spiraling out of control. And it's put things in perspective. Last year in Pennsylvania, we lost through overdose 5,000 Pennsylvanians to opioids and fentanyl, fentanyl being a big part of that. and to put that in perspective. That's more people than were killed in action in Iraq and Afghanistan",
