  {
    "episode_id": 48869,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/8/48869.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 24,
    "turn_text": "those institutions have in many cases evolved in ways. And by the way, those were created under the leadership of the United States, with an explicit set of goals to benefit the world, but also as a way of promoting American values in America's interest. And in many of those cases, we've lost the plot. We've lost the plot. The WHO is the perfect example. So here we have the biggest health crisis in the history of the world. Millions of people dying. It clearly, unequivocally emanates from China. It clearly emanates from Wuhan where there also happens to be a lab that does a lot of experimentation around deadly viruses. And who knows the intentionality? I'm not making any claim. that this was China intentionally did something with COVID. What I am saying is there's clearly, and this is clearly where the COVID originated from, and in combating COVID, we need to get to the root cause of how this happened. And China was essentially refused to provide any transparency and to give any insight into how the virus was created and where it came from and how it was able to spread. And the WHO did its bidding and played no role in trying to create that transparency or accountability. That was the obvious mission and expectation of the World Health Organization. And so I could point to a number of other institutions that have similarly lost their path. And so part of my agenda, my Keystone agenda for America is to essentially look Within the context of US China relations, but more broadly, at a number of these institutions and ask ourselves how they need to be retooled, reformed, in some cases, possibly eliminated. because they've lost their purpose and they certainly aren't fulfilling their original mission.",
