  {
    "episode_id": 48869,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/8/48869.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 27,
    "turn_text": "So when it comes to decoupling from China, what are the immediate challenges that occurs to me is the debt. And it's sort of crazy because I remember people freaking out about how much debt we owed China over a decade ago when I was in middle school. And no one really did anything about it. It's been over a decade. There's not, I mean, our economy hasn't exactly collapsed yet, but there is still kind of worry about it as tensions between the US and China continue to escalate. Is that something that we should be worried about?",
