    "turn_text": "the private capitalism is not imposing a discipline on many of those companies that it imposes in the United States. And that's why you see these government subsidized firms, these state-owned enterprises, that in some ways they're on life support, but continue because they don't have to pay the actual market-driven cost of capital, they're subsidized, they're just, and they distort the economy in a certain number of ways. That is why China doesn't have the resilience and the ability to respond to changes in the global economy and domestic economy the way that the United States does. And a good example of that was COVID. So the way that the American economy came through COVID was in large part just indicative of the American economy in general, which it deals with crisis and disruption in a very fluid and dynamic way. government involvement and so forth, but not nearly to the degree of China and China and the rest of the world have been much slower to recover from COVID because of those dynamics.",
