  {
    "episode_id": 48869,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/8/48869.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 40,
    "turn_text": "Well, listen, Gaza is tragic. I travel with my wife. to Israel right after the new year. We walked through Kafar Azah, which was one of the communities where a hundred people were butchered. We saw the infamous videotape taken from the body camps of the terrorists. I mean, the horrific barbaric evil on that day cannot be, you know, it's unforgettable. And it was not just directed at Israel. That was directed at the West. And my main takeaway from this is, of course, we need to support Israel in its efforts to eliminate Hamas. But that the original sin in all of this was the appeasement of Iran. And it begins with the 2015 deal that President Biden did with Iran, the nuclear deal. Joe Biden supported that, of course, and the deciding vote on it was my opponent in my Senate race, Bob Casey. And that essentially gave Iran more than $100 billion of resources, which it is clearly used to underwrite terror throughout the Middle East. Hamas, Hezbollah, Islamic Jihad, the Houthis, all of these are Iranian proxies that are conducting terrorist operations around the Middle East, and certainly they're not limited in their ambition to the Middle East. And so, Iran's the original sin, and this is where I do hold President Biden and Senator Casey and others accountable because the strategy should have been to call out Iran for what it is, which is the source of the violence terrorist support, and to economically strangle its ability to support terrorist proxies and frankly, both the Obama administration and the Biden administration have failed at that important mission.",
