    "turn_text": "Yeah, boy, it's I mean, I always try to bring it back to to myself if I was in Pennsylvania and thousands of terrorists came across the border from New Jersey and killed women and children in a barbaric way. I wouldn't be able to live in a way that that group could continue to exist 600 meters from my home and put our lives at risk of a day. So I'm wholeheartedly in support of Israel's necessary mission of destroying the Hamas and its ability to ever inflict that kind of evil on Israel. It's a very tough military operation. It's a military man. I know how tough it is because urban warfare, block by block, street by street, building by building room by room is incredibly difficult. It's the most difficult mission. American troops figure that out in Volusia and other places. But then imagine an entire other city underneath the ground",
