    "turn_text": "an incredibly expansive tunnel network. So it's a very tough mission. It's going to have to be conducted. I have a lot of confidence and Israel is a democracy to determine how best to do that. And the Israeli military is an excellent military organization. And I, when I was in Israel, had the chance to sort of see some of it up close and personal. We sat in with a drone unit and talk to their leadership and actually watch them conduct a mission. where they were going through double authentication to make sure that drone targets were truly terrorists. And they wouldn't even rely on a single piece of intel. It had to be multiple sources of intel. So I believe they're conducting this war in a way that is both reflective of their responsibilities under international law and the laws of war, but also in a way that's adding extra measures to try to ensure that the military efforts are targeted against the terrorists. That's made more difficult by the fact that Hamas is integrated itself into the civilian population, which makes it really tricky. Hamas has stood in the way of humanitarian assistance coming to innocent civilians and frankly has blocked those humanitarian corridors. So it's a very tough situation, but I have a lot of confidence his role will manage his way through it.",
