  {
    "episode_id": 48869,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/8/48869.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 45,
    "turn_text": "The way that this has blown up on American University campuses has caused massive nationwide shock. And particularly, I mean, you are running in Pennsylvania, you're a born and raised Pennsylvania, and the University of Pennsylvania, which isn't a state school, but still, just its president just had to step down because of the way that they've handled all of this kind of stuff. Again, it's not a state school. So there's not, I understand that there's not a way you can just jump in and say, no, like stop doing this. But are there ways in which it's possible to hold universities accountable or to change the way that they deal with the way that this is discussed on campus?",
